1	/**
2	 * routes/company-access.ts
3	 *
4	 * CF-native handlers for company-scoped access/membership endpoints:
5	 *   GET /api/companies/:companyId/join-requests
6	 *   GET /api/companies/:companyId/user-directory
7	 *   GET /api/companies/:companyId/members  (if applicable)
8	 *
9	 * The server-side accessRoutes() in access.ts uses raw Express handlers and
10	 * reads bundled SKILL.md files from the host filesystem — neither works in CF.
11	 * These handlers implement the same read-paths directly against the DB.
12	 *
13	 * Auth: requires an authenticated actor (board or agent). Unauthenticated
14	 * requests receive 401. Company-scoped endpoints additionally verify that the
15	 * actor has access to the requested company.
16	 *
17	 * CF-specific caveats:
18	 *   - No filesystem access; all data comes from Hyperdrive/Postgres.
19	 *   - claimSecretHash is always stripped from join-request responses.
20	 */
